            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a semester, then the Malayalam for a syllabus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പാഠ്യപദ്ധതി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പാഠ്യപദ്ധതി — pāṭhyapaddhati — \"a curriculum\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സർക്കാർ പുതിയ പാഠ്യപദ്ധതി കൊണ്ടുവന്നു. sarkkār putiya pāṭhyapaddhati koṇṭuvannu. The government brought in a new curriculum."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പദ്ധതി alone is a plan or a scheme."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പാഠ്യപദ്ധതി (pāṭhyapaddhati) is a Malayalam compound built from Sanskrit pāṭhya, \"to be recited, to be taught\" (Monier-Williams), and paddhati, \"a way, a path\" (Monier-Williams): the path of what is taught."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
