          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഹാജർ (hājar) came from Arabic ḥāḍir, \"present\", and was borrowed from Hindustani hāzir; it is the noun inside ഹാജരാകുക."
